      "content": "You are right to feel that the warning is aggressive; it acts as a safety net because the default slicing behavior often creates a \"view\" that shares memory with the original dataframe, making mutations risky and potentially confusing. While you can silence it using command-line flags like `pd.option_context('mode.chained_assignment', None)`, doing so without resolving the underlying logical error effectively just hides the hidden issue, which can lead to bugs in production code. Attempting to use `.loc` alone won't inherently fix the specific slicing cause, but it will allow you to cleanly assign values before explicitly copying the result with `.copy()` to achieve both memory safety and silence the message reliably.",
